#
# Counter-example for the `math:` expression lowering
# (crates/logic/src/physical/lower.rs,
# MathLoweringError::OccurrenceMultipleDeclaredVariables): a math:VariableExpression
# root whose single math:VariableOccurrence names TWO math:declaredVariable values —
# an occurrence resolves to exactly ONE declaration, so two is ambiguous about which
# declaration it refers to. The authored math:structuralKey lets the reasoned-graph
# gate (check_structural_key_on_rejected_expression) also reach it. Both declarations
# name a math:variableDomain so neither incidentally also trips the unrelated
# math:UntypedFreeVariable constraint — this fixture isolates the ambiguous-declaration
# violation alone.
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:root a math:VariableExpression ;
    math:variableOccurrence ex:occ ;
    math:structuralKey "not-a-real-digest" .

ex:occ a math:VariableOccurrence ;
    math:declaredVariable ex:xFree , ex:yFree .

ex:xFree a math:FreeVariableDeclaration ;
    math:variableDomain math:realNumbers .
ex:yFree a math:FreeVariableDeclaration ;
    math:variableDomain math:realNumbers .
